%description:

Tcp.synLinearTimeouts:doubling -- the timeout of a SYN doubles at each expiry.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "0: the timeout doubles at each expiry (RFC 6298 section 5.5)".

The classes: doubling (0, the default), linear (1 and more; 4 is the value of LinuxTcp). The
code: TcpConnection::process_TIMEOUT_SYN_REXMIT() keeps the timeout of a SYN for this many
retransmissions, and then doubles it. This test separates "doubling" from "linear".

Host under test: host1; the tap drops each SYN. Observation: level 1, the times of the SYNs of
host1: the second 1 s after the first, the third 2 s after the second.

%# parameter: Tcp.synLinearTimeouts
%# class: doubling
%# value: 0
%# key: *.host1.tcp.synLinearTimeouts
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpSynLinearTimeoutsDoubling")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true").drop()
                     .describe("every SYN of host1"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .describe("the first SYN of host1")
                  .within(0.5))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .notBefore(0.99)
                  .describe("the second SYN, 1 s later")
                  .within(1.01))
        .never(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                   .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                   .describe("a SYN less than 2 s after the second")
                   .within(1.9))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
                  .describe("the third SYN, 2 s after the second")
                  .within(0.11));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpSynLinearTimeoutsDoubling compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.synLinearTimeouts = 0    # the parameter under test
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpSynLinearTimeoutsDoubling: PASS
